# hydra-stack seed: what the suite has already absorbed (so hydra-evolve never re-proposes it) and the constitution (protected).
# Imported by setup.py install via `hydra_graph.py seed-import`. One JSON object per line. Source "evolve" = agent lane.
{"kind":"meta_param","title":"Constitution: [V]/[S]/[U] ledger and locator rule","body":"Every load-bearing claim carries V (verified by run/test/authoritative source), S (sourced, attribution verified, truth not) with a locator, or U. Confidence derives from the ledger. Evolution may strengthen this, never weaken it.","conf":"V","tags":"constitution","protected":true}
{"kind":"meta_param","title":"Constitution: red-first test evidence","body":"A passing test earns V only if it was first watched failing. Never-red tests stay U. Spikes exempt but labeled.","conf":"V","tags":"constitution","protected":true}
{"kind":"meta_param","title":"Constitution: concession threshold and frame check","body":"Score a rebuttal 1-5 before conceding; concede at 4+; pushback alone never scores above 2; attack a premise at least once per adversarial pass.","conf":"V","tags":"constitution","protected":true}
{"kind":"meta_param","title":"Constitution: verify before fusing, assert per patch, human gate on skill mutations","body":"Absorb nothing unverified; every patch to a skill asserts its anchor; no shipped skill mutates without the user's approval; attribution and license notes are never condensed away.","conf":"V","tags":"constitution","protected":true}
{"kind":"meta_param","title":"Constitution: one spine per project","body":"GSD, superpowers and GRACE each want to own Plan/Execute. A project picks one; the others stay shelved organs. Never two auto-triggering spines in one repo.","conf":"V","tags":"constitution","protected":true}
{"kind":"meta_param","title":"Constitution: self-owned, model-agnostic, no paid services","body":"Plain files, SQLite, CLI, MCP any client can use. No claude-mem, no Neo4j Aura, no hosted memory by default. Neo4j is an optional self-hosted mirror of graph.db.","conf":"V","tags":"constitution","protected":true}
{"kind":"decision","title":"Absorbed: Spec-Driven Development (BCMS, Popov, 2026-05-11)","body":"REDUNDANT: Specify/Plan/Tasks/Implement, human checkpoints, clarify pass. DELTA adopted into the orchestrator's Specify step: constitution-first, EARS acceptance criteria, out-of-scope section, specs versioned in the repo, spec-first on behaviour change. TENSION: Spec Kit/Kiro are spines, not installed. Its 3-10x and 40h->8h numbers are unsourced: U.","conf":"V","tags":"absorb,sdd"}
{"kind":"decision","title":"Absorbed: Loop & Graph Engineering (Bruniaux, claude-code-ultimate-guide)","body":"DELTA: seven-field loop contract at orchestrator Phase 0; rework budget 2 persisted outside the session; verdict_overturned retro field; three new anti-patterns. NOVEL: graph contract (state schema with named writers, forbidden transitions, checkpoint rule) and admission control in hydra-swarm. REDUNDANT: creator-verifier separation (adversarial-execution), reproduce-before-fix (systematic-debugging), state outside context (STATE.md/baton/graph).","conf":"V","tags":"absorb,loop-graph"}
{"kind":"decision","title":"Absorbed: Anthropic cookbook knowledge-graph guide","body":"REDUNDANT with hydra-graph: typed entities/relations, per-document provenance, entity resolution by normalized key, cite-the-edge answers. DELTA deferred-not-dead: Claude-run entity resolution (cluster surface forms per type with descriptions) and a gold-set P/R/F1 eval for extraction - belongs to research-harvest-verified when it targets graph.db. Its in-memory NetworkX graph and no-confidence-field schema are weaker than graph.db (conf, trust, status, audit chain).","conf":"V","tags":"absorb,knowledge-graph"}
{"kind":"decision","title":"Absorbed: neo4j-skills (neo4j-contrib, MIT, @309e908)","body":"TENSION with the stdlib/self-owned rule as a store; adopted as an optional self-hosted MIRROR: `hydra_graph.py export --format neo4j` emits Cypher 25 idempotent MERGE (no shortestPath; SHORTEST 1 and quantified paths in the example reads). 33 skills shelved and slotted; Aura (paid) skills flagged off-by-default.","conf":"V","tags":"absorb,neo4j"}
{"kind":"decision","title":"Absorbed: GRACE 4 (osovv/grace-marketplace @70f5ec4)","body":"A third contract-first spine with .grace/ XML artifacts. grace-ask (the mcpmarket 'project expert'), grace-status, grace-explainer are organs; the rest are spine-level and shelved. NOVEL deferred-not-dead: a grace-import reading .grace/graph/index.xml into graph.db.","conf":"V","tags":"absorb,grace"}
{"kind":"decision","title":"Absorbed: ponytail (DietrichGebert @09c434a) and karpathy-guidelines (multica-ai @2c60614)","body":"Both are coding-style organs for Execute (ponytail-review/audit/debt slot into Verify/Plan/Learn). karpathy installed-tier (630 tokens); ponytail shelved because its SessionStart hook injects ~3.5 KB per session. Their benchmark numbers are vendor single-project reports: U.","conf":"V","tags":"absorb,style"}
{"kind":"decision","title":"Absorbed: superpowers (obra @b739a8a) and GSD Core 1.18.0 (@199ef8a)","body":"superpowers: 15 skills shelved and slotted; using-superpowers is a rival auto-triggering spine. GSD 1.18 adds .planning/ROADMAP.md, NN-LEARNINGS.md (gsd:extract-learnings), graphs/graph.json (gsd:graphify), mempalace memory and a read-injection scanner hook; hydra-graph imports LEARNINGS and graphs via gsd-import and leaves mempalace (Claude-Code-only) optional.","conf":"V","tags":"absorb,gsd,superpowers"}
{"kind":"decision","title":"Absorbed: Design plugin (7 skills) and setup-audit","body":"Design slots one per station: critique/user-research/research-synthesis -> Discuss; design-system -> Plan; ux-copy -> Execute; accessibility-review -> Verify; design-handoff -> Ship; all shelved (loaded for UI work). setup-audit installed-tier: ops after install and when cost rises, Plan as the agent-readiness check on /gsd-onboard, Learn via repeated-mistake findings.","conf":"V","tags":"absorb,design,setup-audit"}
{"kind":"failed_path","title":"Deferred-not-dead: grace-import, Claude-run entity resolution, extraction eval","body":"Not built in 0.2.0: reading .grace/graph/index.xml into graph.db; an entity-resolution pass over graph node titles; a gold-set P/R/F1 eval for research-harvest-verified. Deferred for scope, not rejected.","conf":"V","tags":"deferred"}
